# The generated OpenAPI spec is committed on purpose.
#
# It was ignored originally because a committed copy drifts from the #[OA\...]
# attributes it was generated from. That reasoning does not hold on Vercel:
# the function filesystem is read-only at runtime except for /tmp, and the
# community vercel-php runtime gives no reliable hook to generate the spec
# during the build. If the file is not in the repository, /api/documentation
# 404s while every other endpoint works.
#
# The cost is that the spec can go stale. Regenerate and commit it:
#
#   php artisan l5-swagger:generate
#
# docs/10-deploying.md explains the tradeoff and the Docker alternative that
# lets the file go back in the ignore list.
!.gitignore
!api-docs.json
!api-docs.yaml
